      "id": "img-no-backslash-authority",
      "md": "![shot](https://github.com\\@evil.com/x.png)",
      "expect": {
        "noTags": [
          "img"
        ],
        "textContains": "shot"
      },
      "note": "markdown escaping turns \\@ into @ before the URL is ever parsed, so this arrives as credentials-in-authority and is rejected. Outside markdown a backslash would end the authority and the host really would be github.com — the URL API handles that too, which is why this is not a regex."
